expected_issues.description:
Failure-path robustness: this debug log dereferences `clusterService.localNode().getId()` and `request.shardId()` while already handling an exception. If `localNode()` is null during startup/shutdown, logging will throw and could mask the original failure or change behavior. Consider null-safe node id / shard id extraction (or log `clusterService.state().nodes().getLocalNodeId()` if guaranteed) and avoid any additional failure points here.

```suggestion
                final String nodeId = clusterService != null && clusterService.localNode() != null ? clusterService.localNode().getId() : "_unknown";
                final Object shardId = request != null ? request.shardId() : "_unknown";
                logger.debug(() -> format("[%s]%s Clearing stack trace before transport:", nodeId, shardId), e);
```

